From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Darren Shepherd <darren@obot.ai>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 12:07:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test(control): pin the settings translation found by hand

Six regression tests over the settings -> ghostty config translation. Each
rule they pin came out of a bug found in manual testing rather than review:
a font family with a space needs the config file's quoting, WT's "infinite"
scrollback is a negative number that must not be forwarded, and ghostty's
padding has to be zero because Windows Terminal already insets the pane -
the double inset is what looked like a border round the first working pane.

To make that testable the translation moves out of GhosttyControlCore into
its own translation unit: it is a pure function over IControlSettings, so
compiled into the test binary it needs no engine, no GPU and no pty. The
rest of the core needs a live surface and stays out of reach of a unit test.

ControlInteractivity.h no longer includes GhosttyControlCore.h - only the
engine factory in the .cpp builds one, and the header was dragging ghostty.h
into every consumer, the unit tests included.

Mutation-verified: unquoting the font family, forwarding a negative history,
padding of 1, and dropping the '#' from a colour each fail exactly one test
and nothing else. unitControl 38/38, unitSettingsModel 159/159.
